/**
 * @file
 * @brief The Build System module documentation.
 *
 * @author Pierre-Henri WUILLEMIN(@LIP6) & Christophe GONZALES(@AMU)
 */

/**
 * \defgroup build_system_group Build System
 * \ingroup technical_topics_group
 *
 * aGrUM/pyAgrum are built with CMake, driven through a thin Python wrapper
 * called `act` (`acttools/`). This page lists the build flavors `act` can
 * produce; for how modules map to shared/static binaries, see
 * \ref modularization_group.
 *
 * \section build_system_act The `act` command
 *
 * Canonical form: `act <action> <mode> <target> [flags...]`
 * - action: `lib`, `install`, `pipinstall`, `test`, `doc`, `wheel`,
 *   `nightly_wheel`, `package`, `guideline`, `clean`, `purge`, `show`
 * - mode: `debug` or `release`
 * - target: `aGrUM` or `pyAgrum` (case-insensitive)
 *
 * Examples: `act lib release aGrUM`, `act test debug pyAgrum`,
 * `act install release aGrUM --static_lib`.
 *
 * `act --dry-run` prints the resulting `cmake` invocation without running
 * it -- the fastest way to see exactly which flags a given combination of
 * options produces.
 *
 * \section build_system_flavors Build flavors
 *
 * <table>
 * <tr><th>Flavor</th><th>CMake option</th><th>`act` flag</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
 * <tr><td>Shared vs static</td><td>`BUILD_SHARED_LIBS` (default `ON`)</td>
 *     <td>`--static_lib`</td>
 *     <td>aGrUM on Windows is always static (enforced by `act`); pyAgrum is
 *     always forced static regardless of this flag.</td></tr>
 * <tr><td>Threading</td><td>`GUM_THREADS=omp|stl` (CMake default `stl`)</td>
 *     <td>`-tt`/`--threads {omp,stl}` (`act` default `omp`)</td>
 *     <td>pyAgrum always forces `GUM_THREADS=stl`.</td></tr>
 * <tr><td>Module selection</td><td>`BUILD_ALL`, `BUILD_<MODULE>`</td>
 *     <td>`-m`/`--modules {show|all|mod1+mod2+...}`</td>
 *     <td>Modules: `BASE`, `BN`, `PRM`, `MRF`, `CN`, `FMDP`, `ID`, `CM`,
 *     `KTBN` (see `src/modules.txt`). pyAgrum additionally toggles each
 *     SWIG-wrapped leaf module independently via
 *     `PYAGRUM_WITH_<MODULE>` (`MRF`, `ID`, `CN`, `CM`, `PRM`, `KTBN`,
 *     default `ON` each); `FMDP` has no Python binding.</td></tr>
 * <tr><td>Database support</td><td>`USE_NANODBC` (default `ON`)</td>
 *     <td>`--withSQL` / `--withoutSQL`</td>
 *     <td>ODBC connectivity via the vendored nanodbc library.</td></tr>
 * <tr><td>Python stable ABI</td><td>`AGRUM_PYTHON_SABI` (default `ON`)</td>
 *     <td>`--stable_abi_off`</td>
 *     <td>Mutually exclusive with the free-threaded build below.</td></tr>
 * <tr><td>Python free-threading</td><td>`AGRUM_PYTHON_NOGIL` (default `OFF`)</td>
 *     <td>`--no_gil`</td>
 *     <td>Experimental GIL-disabled pyAgrum build.</td></tr>
 * <tr><td>Compiler</td><td>n/a</td>
 *     <td>`--compiler {gcc|clang|mvsc22|mvsc19|mvsc17|mvsc15|mingw64|...}`</td>
 *     <td>Default `gcc` on Linux/macOS, `mvsc22` on Windows; only the MSVC
 *     variants and `mingw64` are allowed on Windows.</td></tr>
 * </table>
 *
 * Platforms exercised by the build system: Linux, macOS and Windows, with
 * GCC, Clang and MSVC/MinGW as the supported compiler families (see the
 * top-level `CLAUDE.md` for the minimum supported versions).
 */
